1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,180
Adding a book used to mean typing everything.

2
00:00:03,180 --> 00:00:08,740
Now Nia starts typing a title, and matching books drop down under it, each with its cover.

3
00:00:10,679 --> 00:00:11,922
She picks The Hobbit.

4
00:00:11,922 --> 00:00:17,660
The author and the cover fill in by themselves, and she only has to say how many chapters it has.

5
00:00:19,879 --> 00:00:23,620
When the catalogue has nothing, Shelfie offers guesses instead.

6
00:00:23,620 --> 00:00:28,429
Each one is marked Suggested, with a reminder to check it before adding the book.

7
00:00:30,559 --> 00:00:36,339
If the lookup ever fails, a short note says so, and Nia can carry on typing the book in herself.

